  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced. Cut potato into fries.\n• Place fries on a lined oven tray.\n• Drizzle with olive oil, season with salt and toss to coat. Bake until tender, 20-25 minutes.\n• While the fries are baking, thinly slice brown onion. In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Add onion and cook, stirring, until softened, 5-6 minutes.\n• Add the balsamic vinegar, brown sugar and a splash of water, and mix well. Reduce heat to medium and cook until dark and sticky, 3-5 minutes. Transfer to a small bowl.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f878e40d0527cba53bf283/step-52fac600.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the onions are caramelising, thinly slice tomato.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f878e40d0527cba53bf283/step-8a35e810.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Wash out frying pan and return to a medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook plant-based burger patties until browned and heated through, 2-3 minutes each side.\n• In the last 1-2 minutes of cook time, sprinkle Cheddar cheese over the patties, then cover with a lid so the cheese melts.\n• While the patties are cooking, place bake-at home burger buns on a wire rack in the oven for 3 minutes, or until heated through. TIP: For even browning, gently press down on the patties using a spatula.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f878e40d0527cba53bf283/step-bba6e520.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Slice burger buns in half. Spread each bun with some BBQ mayo.\n• Top with a plant-based burger patty, caramelised onion, tomato and mixed salad leaves.\n• Serve with the fries and remaining BBQ mayo. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f878e40d0527cba53bf283/step-0c4ef130.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
